    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52690" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλλιον</span></b>  (B), τό,
		precinct used as a Court at Athens, <i><span class="en">
			<u>AB</u>
			269
		</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
			Androt.
		</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
			Poll.
			8.121
		</span></i> (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάλλειον</span></b> , fr.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλίας</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Phot.
		</span></i>); at Cyzicus, apptly. a <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>board</i> or <i>bench of magistrates</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρχων τοῦ κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.153
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλιάζω,
				καλλιαρχέω</span>.</div>
